  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, numerically stable reference implementation following exact specifications.\n\n### 💻 Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport math\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef roi_pool(feature_map: list, rois: list, output_size: int) -> list:\n    fm = np.array(feature_map, dtype=float)\n    pooled = []\n    for roi in rois:\n        x1, y1, x2, y2 = roi\n        roi_h = max(1, y2 - y1)\n        roi_w = max(1, x2 - x1)\n        bin_h = roi_h / output_size\n        bin_w = roi_w / output_size\n        roi_out = np.zeros((output_size, output_size), dtype=float)\n        for i in range(output_size):\n            for j in range(output_size):\n                h_start = int(math.floor(y1 + i * bin_h))\n                h_end = int(math.ceil(y1 + (i + 1) * bin_h))\n                w_start = int(math.floor(x1 + j * bin_w))\n                w_end = int(math.ceil(x1 + (j + 1) * bin_w))\n                patch = fm[h_start:h_end, w_start:w_end]\n                roi_out[i, j] = np.max(patch) if patch.size > 0 else 0.0\n        pooled.append(np.round(roi_out, 6).tolist())\n    return pooled\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for memory buffers.\n",
